go 1.25.0

// go.work is committed on purpose. The three modules in this repository
// depend on each other (web -> core, examples -> web -> core) and none of
// them is published yet, so without a workspace neither web nor examples can
// resolve the core module at all -- `go build ./...` in web fails outright.
// The alternative, a local `replace` in each sub-module, is exactly what must
// not happen: a replace directive travels with the published module and would
// break every downstream consumer, and it would also hide the one property
// these modules have to keep proving, that they resolve as ordinary tagged
// dependencies. Once core and web are tagged this file stops being load-
// bearing and becomes a convenience for local development.
use (
	.
	./examples
	./web
)
